# A row batch of two rows of the `entry` table of schemas/exchange.schema
# (document 05 section 1, "Row batches"), as hex bytes; `#` starts a comment.
# Each row struct is 61 bytes: id Id128 (16), user_id u64 (8), asset u32 (4),
# kind Enum8 (1), amount Decimal(38, 18) as an i128 mantissa (16), ref Id128 (16).
# The table has no String or Bytes column, so the heap is empty.

02 00 00 00  # count: 2 rows
00 00 00 00  # reserved

# Row 0, at offset 8: a credit of 100.5 of asset 1 for user 7.
01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 1c 2a 5b 93 01  # id
07 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  # user_id 7
01 00 00 00  # asset 1
00  # kind 0, credit
00 00 c2 36 87 b9 b7 72 05 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  # amount 100.5
f1 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 1c 2a 5b 93 01  # ref

# Row 1, at offset 69: a debit of 0.25 of asset 1 for user 7.
02 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 1c 2a 5b 93 01  # id
07 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  # user_id 7
01 00 00 00  # asset 1
01  # kind 1, debit
00 00 d9 e9 ac 2d 78 03 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00  # amount 0.25
f2 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 1c 2a 5b 93 01  # ref
